Subject: [PATCH] regulator: add SGM3851A SWIRE voltage control

Drive the enable pins at probe and keep the chip at its default
voltages unless a startup pulse sequence is configured in firmware.
Allow userspace to set all three outputs in signed microvolts using
the discrete voltages from the SGM3851A data sheet.

Serialize commands with shutdown and mask local interrupts during
each non-sleeping SWIRE frame.

diff --git a/drivers/regulator/Kconfig b/drivers/regulator/Kconfig
index d84f3d054..fdbccecad 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/regulator/Kconfig
@@ -440,6 +440,15 @@ config REGULATOR_FAN53880
 	  (PMIC), it is controlled by I2C and provides one BUCK, one BOOST
 	  and four LDO outputs.
 
+config REGULATOR_SGM3851A
+	tristate "SGMicro SGM3851A display bias supply"
+	depends on OF && GPIOLIB
+	help
+	  Enable the SGM3851A AMOLED outputs through their GPIOs and optionally
+	  program the output voltages over SWIRE on CTRL. The device powers up
+	  at its factory voltages unless a startup sequence is specified.
+	  Programming requires a non-sleeping GPIO for timed SWIRE commands.
+
 config REGULATOR_GPIO
 	tristate "GPIO regulator support"
 	depends on GPIOLIB || COMPILE_TEST
